WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:08.070
This is the same fusion stack, pointed outward instead of forward, the PS-16 perimeter console.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:14.070
Radar, thermal and camera tracks along the fence line are classified individually and then correlated.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:20.070
Watch two separate contacts become one threat, a vehicle loitering on the access road

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.070
and a person who dismounts and approaches the fence. Neither would raise an alarm alone.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:31.070
The ladder on the right is the escalation state, loiter, approach, breach risk,

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:35.070
so the operator sees intent forming rather than an alarm at the moment of breach.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:41.070
The console states its reasoning in words, and the feature that matters most is restraint.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:48.070
Benign tracks are held, never escalated. False alarm rate is what gets a perimeter system switched off.
